{#
  Apparatus finder-mark social card.

  Lives in the user head slot (auto-discovered by src/site/_data/dynamics.js) so
  it adds no template-owned divergence. See design.md "Template-owned divergences".

  Per-note `metatags` in frontmatter already emit og:title / og:description /
  og:type via pageheader.njk, but nothing sets an image. This supplies the
  site-wide default card and only fills gaps — a note that sets its own
  og:image in metatags wins.

  The card is fixed to DL's cream-paper palette regardless of the reader's
  theme preference. Social crawlers do not reliably follow theme preferences.
#}
{%- set explicitOgImage = metatags["og:image"] if metatags and metatags["og:image"] else "" -%}
{%- set apparatusCard = explicitOgImage | apparatusOgImage(noteProps, page.fileSlug, categories, meta.siteBaseUrl) -%}
{%- if not explicitOgImage -%}
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ apparatusCard }}">
{%- endif -%}
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ apparatusCard }}">
